i gotta admit  given what we've seen over the last six  months i thought we were witnessing the  end of the division franchise  but then suddenly out of the blue today  or tomorrow depending on when i actually  managed to release this we receive an  announcement from ubisoft  saying that not only is the division  going to be hanging around but it will  be expanding  into what they are calling a division  universe  this isn't just an update to the  division 2 but a separate standalone  addition to the world  ubisoft released an update on social  media discussing their new title  the division heartland  [Music]  i won't read through the article word  for word i just want to talk to some of  the points they've raised  mainly because i'm bloody excited and  feel the need to talk to it  but i have a link to the original story  in the description  they started out by talking around the  high ambitions they still have around  the division ip  that the success around the title has  led to a community of over 40 million  players  and that this had set up the franchise  to move on a trajectory that would  include more games  and more transmedia content set within  the division universe  now we already know of the new content  being created for the division 2  hopefully later on this year  but there has been other ubisoft teams  exploring additional ways to introduce  the division to even more players  and this is where the concept behind the  division heartland grew from  heartland is a free-to-play game set in  the division universe  being developed by redstorm studio they  went on to say that heartland  is a standalone game that doesn't  require previous experience within the  series  but will provide an all-new perspective  on the universe in a new setting  so no previous experience in the  franchise is required  it will provide an all-new perspective  and it's free to play  details are particularly slim but even  with the small amount of information  we've received so  far we can speculate because that seems  to be what we do here  are they following the now dated trend  of creating a battle royale  the development has been led by redstorm  entertainment a studio with close ties  to the tom clancy licenses  who have also worked on the division and  the division two  redstone does have a history of working  on the division pvp in earlier days  and this would certainly make the pvp  crowd happy maybe it will be a spin-off  of the survival mode  this has certainly been something the  community has been most disappointed  about  and not seeing the continuation of will  it be a looter shooter  and skill based or maybe we'll be seeing  some sort of large-scale mmo  or a single-player story narrative as  was talked about quite some time ago by  one of the divs  will this new game even be canon  continuing with the story  or branching off in some sort of way  based on the name of the game and the  image alone with the large water tower  overlooking a landscape  of low flat rolling terrain it wouldn't  be unreasonable to assume that heartland  will be based in the american midwest  the kenaid and fellow division addict  maverick  not only pointed out that michigan is in  this region of the us and that this is  the location of the events that took  place at the end of the broken door  novel with april kalahar  she even points out that ann arbor also  has a large water tower  overlooking the settlement  but i would be surprised if it was a  game with a full-on campaign  like we've seen from the other two  whatever they're planning  i expect there'll be continued focus on  the core of what the division is  being one of the major early entries  into the luda shooter genre  i don't think we'll be seeing a  dedicated battle royale pvp mode of the  game  this isn't what the division is known  for where the story  gameplay and pve elements have been what  has driven the franchise  and the bulk of the player base up until  now sorry pvp players i could be wrong  but it just doesn't make sense to me  however there are rumors that this is  the reason that we never saw survival  make it into the second game  regardless of the direction heartland is  set to release in 2021 2022  on pc and console however you can sign  up for early testing now so hopefully  we'll get to see something soon  i'm obviously very excited to see that  division is not just still being worked  on  but has another standalone game coming  out though as it's a free-to-play game  i'm interested to see how their  monetization model will work  but heartland wasn't the only new  development in the tom clancy universe  they also talked about a division mobile  game coming out  i'm not necessarily much of a mobile  gamer but the increase in audience and  awareness of the division name  certainly won't be a bad thing for its  future and as well as the movie that's  currently being created  we'll also be getting a new original  novel  so what is to come for the franchise  updates to the division 2  with emphasis on a new method for  levelling agents and an increase in  build variety and viability  a movie a novel and a new free-to-play  game  called heartland i think it's pretty  safe to say that the division isn't  dying  and in fact is setting up for a long  future in the industry  as i said i'll post a link to the full  article in the description  hopefully you're as happy as i am to see  some sort of a future for the division  and if you're not you're absolutely  watching the wrong videos  anyway thanks for watching and i'll  catch you in the next one cheers  [Applause]  [Music]  uh

